To emit a complete vFinal I would have to write the majority of it from plausible inference. That is the failure mode the no-new-noun rule and *silence must never become specification* were built to prevent, applied to the highest-leverage artifact in the system. A spec that looks committable and is 80% invented is worse than no spec, because the invented parts read with the same authority as the real ones.

So the merge is yours to perform, or mine with the text in hand.

